# Machine-local cargo config — COPY to `.cargo/config.toml` (git-ignored) and
# edit for your machine. Do NOT commit `.cargo/config.toml`: an absolute path
# here breaks every other checkout and the CI build cache (Swatinem/rust-cache
# expects the default `target/`).
#
# When you need it: the `v8` crate's build.rs creates a Windows symlink when the
# cargo target dir and the cargo registry live on different drives (e.g. target
# on D: but registry on C:), which fails without Developer Mode. Pinning the
# target dir to the registry's drive avoids it.
#
# [build]
# target-dir = "C:/Users/<you>/.cache/baston-target"
